course: dictionary
lesson: 11172
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. «Winged» is one of these words. In «a winged horse», winged means having wings, because the horse is a flying creature in a story.
explain: Winged can also be the past of the verb wing. «The arrow winged the bird» means the arrow hit the bird lightly in the wing or arm. Read the whole sentence before you decide what it means.
explain: Some phrases are informal, so you cannot work them out one word at a time. «I winged the speech» means I did it without preparing, making it up as I went along. To wing it means to do something on the spot. Ask yourself: is this about a thing with wings, or about how someone did something?
fact: Winged means having wings, as in «a winged horse» or a winged dragon.
fact: Winged can also be the past of wing: «The arrow winged the bird» means it hit the bird lightly in the wing or arm.
fact: To have winged it means you did something without preparing, making it up as you went along.
fact: «Sycamore seeds have a wing that makes them spin as they fall, slowing them down.» Sycamore is a kind of maple.
fact: In compound words, -winged describes the type of wings, as in «long-winged» or «red-winged blackbird».
exercise: «The old story tells of a winged horse.» What does winged mean here? | *Having wings | Made of wood | Covered in mud | Very fast and quick
exercise: «The arrow winged the bird.» What does winged mean here? | Caught the bird in a net | *Hit the bird lightly in the wing or arm | Painted the bird's feathers | Flew past the bird
exercise: Ella says, «I winged the speech.» What does she mean? | She practised it for a week | *She did it without preparing, making it up as she went along | She gave it while sitting down | She sang it instead
test: «The red-winged blackbird sat on the fence.» In red-winged, what does -winged describe? | The size of the fence | *The type of wings | A colour | A sound
test: Jayden says, «I'll just wing it.» What does wing it mean? | Fly away quickly | Practise the same thing again and again | Hurt someone's arm | *Do it without preparing, making it up
exam: Read this: «Sycamore seeds have a wing that makes them spin as they fall.» What does the sentence tell you about sycamore seeds? | *They spin as they fall, which slows them down | They grow only in the summer | They sink straight down like stones | They can fly like birds
